=20

The Book chapter 18:

8.10)  mi citka pino'o lei nanba

I eat a-typical-amount-of the-mass-of bread.=20


The translation seems to me not correct. Or am I again misreading some
principle?

"the-mass-of" sounds more like {ro}, as in:

8.8)  mi citka piro lei nanba

I eat the-whole-of the-mass-of bread


and {pi} sounds more like "the-whole-of", as in, in addition to the
above one:=20

piso'a  PA+PA   almost the whole of


What distinguishes {ro} and {pi}, according to the Book, is the
difference between "elements of totality" and "part of a whole",
respectively.=20


mu'o mi'e vid


